                        ],
                        "form": "bréhaignes"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "92e85aaa-ab80-4e29-b316-d01a6cbb4277",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "brehaine"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2add259f-f8e3-4518-8d4f-a15e3d5357aa",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "brehaigne"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c1c54458-145f-391a-9cc3-ed5b9c18a1db",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stérile, en parlant des femelles de certains animaux."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aea25b7c-b39c-402e-9b03-1f108a0f6649",
                                "sense_id": "c1c54458-145f-391a-9cc3-ed5b9c18a1db",
                                "text": "A Mervale, les vieilles biques bréhaignes cabretaient sans besoin de bouc, les petits poussaient sur les fumiers !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32d67589-c660-3f57-9ba8-08007ec6363a",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualifie un poisson qui n’a ni œufs ni laitance."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6112e47-a465-474d-93fe-aaf4fe495197",
                                "sense_id": "32d67589-c660-3f57-9ba8-08007ec6363a",
                                "text": "Duhamel pense aussi que les carpes qu’on nomme bréhaignes ne sont point des mulets, mais des poissons qui, dans certaines circonstances, sont dépourvus de laitance et d’œufs."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f7d49faa-19cf-3a2f-a88e-142af2922293",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "(Souvent ironique) Stérile, en parlant d’une femme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b01e8c87-2118-4ad1-b0e0-aaac184fbbbe",
                                "sense_id": "f7d49faa-19cf-3a2f-a88e-142af2922293",
                                "text": "Elle meublait de menues pratiques pieuses sa monotone vie déçue, et, bréhaigne, donnait à l’idéal les soins que ne réclamait d’elle aucun enfant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9c95711-fba4-4b5c-a58f-b29cc620d4e7",
                                "sense_id": "f7d49faa-19cf-3a2f-a88e-142af2922293",
                                "text": "20 avril 43 – Il y a parfois dans les familles de ces cousines bréhaignes, providence des veufs et cerbères de logis qui ne leur appartiennent jamais que par accident."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56098b70-758f-4de4-90fc-2c2fa0ca0a82",
                                "sense_id": "f7d49faa-19cf-3a2f-a88e-142af2922293",
                                "text": "Cette prouesse médicale se payait cependant au prix fort : Marguerite n’aurait plus jamais d’enfant. […] Sous le coup de la déception, Lucien n’avait pas trouvé les mots qui auraient pu apaiser le chagrin de Marguerite, devenue bréhaigne à vingt ans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "506375c5-5862-48da-bedc-8e0edf11f25f",
                                "sense_id": "f7d49faa-19cf-3a2f-a88e-142af2922293",
                                "text": "Je vous parie une vache pleine contre une dame bréhaigne qu’il se prépare des choses pas décorticables pour bientôt !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6dd681d1-c49d-322f-b7eb-11ce39f1db36",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est stérile, ne contient aucune vie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aec5c2a-b583-401e-95fb-d4d50c8e1af3",
                                "sense_id": "6dd681d1-c49d-322f-b7eb-11ce39f1db36",
                                "text": "Tout est déréglé, la nature (la mer devient bréhaigne), les lois (il n’est plus permis de porter secours), la famille (le conseil des anciens n'est plus écouté), et l'ordre ancien ne reviendra jamais."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e6c767e-2a58-4d7e-9523-47d1ee6405bf",
                                "sense_id": "6dd681d1-c49d-322f-b7eb-11ce39f1db36",
                                "text": "Ce n’est point cependant une terre bréhaigne, puisque ses enfants se comptent par millions, et si cette mère n’a pas de lait pour ses petits, du moins l’aiment-ils passionnément."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c168f91-d0f1-3a8f-8623-fb7f49425ab9",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui partage avec le cheval certaines caractéristiques, en parlant de la jument."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "138c12bd-7cf3-405e-b0e4-c7503611bdee",
                                "sense_id": "1c168f91-d0f1-3a8f-8623-fb7f49425ab9",
                                "text": "[Les crocs ou de crochets sont] les quatre dents canines du cheval, que nos peres appelloient écaillons. Ces quatre dents canines sont celles dont les jumens sont dépourvûes, à l’exception de celles auxquelles nous donnons le nom de brehaigne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e3b8409-2900-4978-9590-2a48def1e1b1",
                                "sense_id": "1c168f91-d0f1-3a8f-8623-fb7f49425ab9",
                                "text": "Les jumens en sont communément privées, & n’ont par conséquent que trente-six dents : il en est néanmoins qui en ont quarante, mais leurs crochets sont toûjours très-petits, & elles sont dites brechaines. Beaucoup de personnes les regardent comme admirables pour le service, & comme très-impropres pour le haras."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "63dfa1b5-67cc-3c4f-a689-43aa623f24b5",
                        "entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bohémien."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Hapax"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "003cc144-2ead-4acf-af3a-39a29d5f17fb",
                                "sense_id": "63dfa1b5-67cc-3c4f-a689-43aa623f24b5",
                                "text": "À l’avant, sur un strapontin adhérent au fourgon et ayant pour porte la fenêtre, au-dessus de la croupe des chevaux, à côté d’un vieillard qui tenait les guides et dirigeait l’attelage, deux femmes bréhaignes, c’est-à-dire bohémiennes, vêtues en déesses, sonnaient de la trompette. L’ébahissement des bourgeois contemplait et commentait cette machine, fièrement cahotante."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cc89da92-4bf0-4dd2-9d3e-c9a3d1d8ec13",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e62b7a0-e6f4-3584-9102-6f7eb2210e23",
                        "source_sense_description": "Stérile",
                        "target_lang_word": "barren",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "barren",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac4983cc-6da4-3d4a-aba5-4065cc604917",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not bearing children, childless; hence also unable to bear children, sterile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "712c3aba-e723-486a-ae70-70a88d5b8570",
                                                "sense_id": "ac4983cc-6da4-3d4a-aba5-4065cc604917",
                                                "text": "I silently wept as my daughter's husband rejected her. What would she do now that she was no longer a maiden but also barren?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f244a960-a992-49f2-8bfd-5fc228137e59",
                                                "sense_id": "ac4983cc-6da4-3d4a-aba5-4065cc604917",
                                                "text": "Forget not, in your speed, Antonius,\nTo touch Calpurnia; for our elders say,\nThe barren, touched in this holy chase,\nShake off their sterile curse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e09d6c5a-50a2-403f-8f5d-5162930e4905",
                                                "sense_id": "ac4983cc-6da4-3d4a-aba5-4065cc604917",
                                                "text": "The druids […] believed that mistletoe could make barren animals fecund, and that it was an antidote to all poisons."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d8fcbb7-b148-3de2-8784-1c9153943ccb",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not bearing seed or fruit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6abf3360-7bde-3ef1-b65a-7fa6dc90a901",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of poor fertility, infertile; not producing vegetation; desert, waste."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of places"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7314976-c66a-46c5-82c0-8cfaad1e9c32",
                                                "sense_id": "6abf3360-7bde-3ef1-b65a-7fa6dc90a901",
                                                "text": "barren mountain tracts"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f1792e8-87a7-4ebf-99dd-c64ea94e01ad",
                                                "sense_id": "6abf3360-7bde-3ef1-b65a-7fa6dc90a901",
                                                "text": "We have descended Tian Shan and entered the Taklamakan Desert, a barren landscape painted in ecru—no shrubs, no grass, only waves upon waves of naked ridges the color of buff, the highest few spotted with white specks of snow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d61b8a6a-ebcb-409e-98e4-626dddeb3df5",
                                                "sense_id": "6abf3360-7bde-3ef1-b65a-7fa6dc90a901",
                                                "text": "Terraforming even a barren planet often involves significant financial and ethical hurdles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "12f8a032-53f4-3ff4-a1f5-463cea1214e4",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Devoid, lacking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "with-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e940856-e16d-42ec-8e06-b20f682248ed",
                                                "sense_id": "12f8a032-53f4-3ff4-a1f5-463cea1214e4",
                                                "text": "August 28, 1731, Jonathan Swift, letter to John Gay\nBut schemes are perfectly accidental. Some will appear barren of hints and matter, but prove to be fruitful."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f861961e-2ed8-3a5c-a8bf-a2ddbe22fe7c",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Devoid of interest or attraction, poor, bleak."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6ee8fb2-b669-46e1-b117-c25f9a194a89",
                                                "sense_id": "f861961e-2ed8-3a5c-a8bf-a2ddbe22fe7c",
                                                "text": "As they turned into Hertford Street they startled a robin from the poet's head on a barren fountain, and he fled away with a cameo note."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unproductive, fruitless, unprofitable; empty, hollow, vain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87461808-77f8-406c-815e-3916900dacc5",
                                                "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                                "text": "brilliant but barren reveries"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03211b0b-2817-42c8-990c-739dd0b5b575",
                                                "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                                "text": "A third is wroth: ‘Is this an hour\n⁠For private sorrow’s barren song,\n⁠When more and more the people throng\nThe chairs and thrones of civil power?’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f548e70-6e57-4c69-961f-f0ab30c8640c",
                                                "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                                "text": "When the entire coast-line becomes a sea of waving palms, with Chinese and Malay villages fringing the shores, which are at present mere barren wastes of mangroves, with plantations of pepper, of gambier, and of tapioca and rice, the Northern Territory, backed up by the unswerving energy of the Australian squatter, miner, and planter, will present a spectacle almost unknown in the scheme of British colonization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3edd220-2ba3-4c28-8ede-08cd007fba7c",
                                                "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                                "text": "Rooney had been suffered a barren spell for England with only one goal in 15 games but he was in no mood to ignore the gifts on offer in front of an increasingly subdued Bulgarian support."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fb24d07-1a77-4406-b03c-cd96409b4f1e",
                                                "sense_id": "7b616cb9-20fb-3b3f-a59a-e3afb9a6c25d",
                                                "text": "As the glut of new orders placed in the optimistic pre-pandemic years (worth billions of pounds) reaches its conclusion, production lines in Newton Aycliffe, Derby and Newport face a potentially barren future - as well as job losses that will be devastating for their communities and supply chains."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a96db256-7c2f-380f-8b61-b7814060c70c",
                                        "entry_id": "2f47f8df-b75b-3401-8068-9cdbebf158ff",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mentally dull or unproductive; stupid or intellectually fallow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b9cf337-5164-42e1-a582-50f0526110b8",
                                                "sense_id": "a96db256-7c2f-380f-8b61-b7814060c70c",
                                                "text": "Set on some quantity of barren spectators to laugh too."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "barren",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c68c5163-2eb9-307e-98d6-744d369a6b4f",
                                        "entry_id": "f82ba157-9791-38a4-9955-2505de3f3cdd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An area of low fertility and habitation, a desolate place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a581f47f-8f27-4ecb-95a8-2d9a7e429066",
                                                "sense_id": "c68c5163-2eb9-307e-98d6-744d369a6b4f",
                                                "text": "Sol squinted out over the barrens to where the mountains shimmered in the heat haze."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                        "entry_id": "f82ba157-9791-38a4-9955-2505de3f3cdd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In particular, a usually elevated and flat expanse of land that only supports the growth of small trees and shrubs, and sometimes mosses or heathers, berries, and other marshy or moory vegetation, but little agriculture and few people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "plural-normally"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b34bbb7c-96ba-4039-b1e1-cdfa006ab02c",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "The pine barrens are a site lonely enough to suit any hermit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d48f7bb7-daba-41f3-abc2-9a1c55374dd6",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "Snow Lies now four & five feet deep upon the Ground & the Air looks so Hazey that we think it Prudent to Return upon the Rocks & Barrens (for so they Call the Places where Wood does not Grow) we find that the wind had drifted the Snow Very thin Here we observe Some few Plants (1) Fir Moss, *Lycopodium Selago, (2) Rhein Deer Moss, Lichen Rangiferinus [Cladonia sp.], (3) A Kind of Horned Liverwort, Lichen, (4) a Plant that has very much the Appearance of Crow Berries, Empetrum [*Empetrum nigrum L.] of which I have only got the female which has 10 Stigmata."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ad06608-9c22-4f47-a871-7730e76f55d0",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "Here it was now, by the side of a Swamp in the Barrens of Newfoundland, threadbare, wet, dirty."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df5cf57e-c0a7-42fa-89b4-a23a38268c4a",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "What is known of it consists of a rocky and barren soil, steep hills covered with bad wood, some narrow and sandy valleys, extensive plains covered either with heath, or with rocky surfaces, more or less extensive, where not a tree or shrub is to be seen, and which are from thence usually called Barrens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b6ef328-0572-4406-97b6-782d9fb58189",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "The 'barrens' of Newfoundland are those districts which occupy the summits of the hills and ridges, and other elevated and exposed tracts. They are covered with a thin and scrubby vegetation, consisting of berry-bearing plants and dwarf bushes of various species, and are somewhat similar in appearance to the moorlands of the north of England, differing only in the kind of vegetation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b380849d-99a2-4b6f-bb7a-d6e79e42a4b7",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "In Newfound-land there are barrens of many miles in extent, high, and, comparatively speaking, dry plateaus; but the barrens in the provinces I am speaking of vary from a little open space of a few acres to a plain of five or six miles[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2feddbe-cca0-4d32-8f25-c974b0fd6b41",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "The 'barrens' are covered with a rich carpet of moss of every shade and colour, and abound in all sorts of wild berries, pleasing both to the eye and taste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57b36e86-243b-46c8-9a2c-aa01fccf6913",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "[...] the Arctic strip extends from the exposed coasts of the outer islands, in onto the mainland for from one to three or four miles as a practically unbroken \"barren,\" sprinkled with lichen-covered ledges and carpeted with turf of reindeer lichen, sphagnum, Empetrum, sedges, creeping willows, and various other species of herbaceous plants, including the following, kindly determined for us by Dr. B. L. Robinson of the Gray herbarium[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a8d46c5-ee66-46e3-8d33-b3fc6d85dd78",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "No pan is more rugged and inhospitable than these 'barrens,' the vast rolling plateaux of the interior, broken by stunted groups of wind-tom trees Only at the plateaux' edges."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a466d0fd-b5de-494e-a03e-16ba00fa9bcc",
                                                "sense_id": "bf65ff4d-4f12-37ab-a157-c40da07db688",
                                                "text": "Habitat: Bogs, Heaths (known as 'Barrens' in Newfoundland) and rough meadows near boglands. Range In the eastern area: Manitoba eastward; including northern Minnesota to Newfoundland (A.B. Klots)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
